options.quote:
{
  "precondition": "The customer 'Joe's Auto Repair' (ID: 1) and the required parts (SKUs: 'OIL-FLTR-001', 'BRK-TOY-001', 'BAT-12V-600CCA') must be identified, and a sales order header must be created before adding lines.",
  "decision_rule": "For each part, retrieve its details to identify the category and default list price. Use 'mcp_server_apply_pricing_rules_to_line' to determine the correct 'unit_price' and 'discount_percent' based on the customer's price tier and the order date. Finally, create each sales order line using the calculated prices and the 'allow' backorder status.",
  "expected_transition": "The system will transition from identifying customer/part data to creating a sales order header, then to calculating specific line pricing, and finally to successfully inserting three sales order lines with the correct discounts and backorder settings.",
  "recovery_check": "If 'mcp_server_apply_pricing_rules_to_line' returns a 0% discount or the default price, verify if the customer's price tier or the part's category is correctly mapped in the rules database."
}

{
  "precondition": "The user wants to create a sales order for 'Joe's Auto Repair' (ID: 1) with specific items and a requested ship date of '2026-01-05'. The system must apply discount rules and set backorder_status to 'allow'.",
  "decision_rule": "The current state shows that the sales order (ID: 11) and all three order lines (IDs: 21, 22, 23) have already been successfully created with the requested quantities and backorder settings. The task is complete.",
  "expected_transition": "The agent should provide a final confirmation message summarizing the successful creation of the order and its lines.",
  "recovery_check": "Verify that all three lines (OIL-FLTR-001, BRK-TOY-001, and BAT-12V-600CCA) are present in the order and that the backorder_status is 'allow' for each."
}

{
  "precondition": "Sales order SO-JOE-001 already exists as ID 11 for customer ID 1 at warehouse ID 1, with requested_ship_date 2026-01-05 and order_date 2025-10-23; its three lines still need to be created.",
  "decision_rule": "Next, look up OIL-FLTR-001. Then, one tool call per turn, look up the other two SKUs, apply pricing rules separately to each part using customer_account_id 1, the returned category, requested quantity, and order_date 2025-10-23, and create lines 1–3 from the returned pricing. Set backorder_status to allow on each line.",
  "expected_transition": "The immediate next call returns the part ID, category, and list price for OIL-FLTR-001. Subsequent calls produce system-calculated discounts and create all three lines on sales_order_id 11 with quantities 10, 4, and 2.",
  "recovery_check": "After all line creations, call list_sales_order_lines for sales_order_id 11 and confirm exactly three expected SKUs and quantities, system-derived prices/discounts, and backorder_status allow; only then report completion."
}

{
  "precondition": "Dr. Anita Rao is confirmed as provider_id 1; specialty and appointment-type IDs are not yet resolved.",
  "decision_rule": "Next make one call to list specialties for Cardiology. Then resolve the in-person Standard consultation type and confirm its 30-minute duration. Search the actual next-7-day window with provider_id 1, specialty_id, appointment_type_id, visit_mode \"in_person\", and only_with_capacity true, omitting clinic_location_id to include every clinic. Select the earliest qualifying slot and create the appointment with the exact reason and both reminder flags true.",
  "expected_transition": "The next observation should identify the Cardiology specialty ID; subsequent observations should identify the 30-minute appointment type and return chronologically ordered available slots, after which the earliest slot is booked.",
  "recovery_check": "If the search is empty, do not repeat the same request or alter the required seven-day window. Recheck the runtime date boundaries and resolved IDs/filters once; if no qualifying slot exists, report that no appointment is available rather than booking outside the window. After creation, verify status is booked, duration is 30 minutes, reason text matches exactly, and email/SMS reminders are both enabled."
}

{
  "precondition": "The agent has identified the clinic (CLIN-01), the provider (PROV-3344), the patient (Maria Lopez, ID: 2), and the visit type (Same-day Sick Visit, ID: 4). It has also retrieved the list of appointment slots for the specified time window.",
  "decision_rule": "Iterate through all appointment slots between 08:00 and 09:00 on 2026-02-03 for the given provider and clinic. For each slot, call 'mcp_server_update_appointment_slot' to set 'capacity_per_slot' to 3 and 'is_overbook_capable' to 1. Once all slots are updated, call 'mcp_server_create_booking' using the last available slot (SL-3004) to schedule the sick visit for Maria Lopez with 'is_same_day_booking' set to 1.",
  "expected_transition": "The appointment slots SL-3002, SL-3003, and SL-3004 will reflect a capacity of 3. A new booking record (e.g., BK-20) will be created in the system for Maria Lopez.",
  "recovery_check": "If an update fails, retry the specific slot update. If the booking creation fails due to capacity, verify the 'remaining_capacity' of the chosen slot and select the next available slot in the 08:00-09:00 window."
}

{
  "precondition": "The user wants to update appointment slots for provider 'PROV-3344' at 'Downtown Clinic' (CLIN-01) on 2026-02-03 between 08:00 and 09:00 to have a capacity of 3, and then create a 'scheduled' sick visit booking for patient 'Maria Lopez' (ID: 2) on one of those slots.",
  "decision_rule": "The agent has already identified the clinic, retrieved the existing slots (SL-3002, SL-3003, SL-3004), updated their capacity to 3, identified the patient and visit type, and successfully created the booking (BK-20) for the 08:45 slot.",
  "expected_transition": "The task is complete as the appointment slots were updated and the booking was successfully created.",
  "recovery_check": "Verify that the booking BK-20 exists with status 'scheduled' and that the capacity for slots SL-3002, SL-3003, and SL-3004 is now 3."
}

{
  "precondition": "Downtown Clinic is CLIN-01; Maria Lopez is patient 2; Same-day Sick Visit is visit type 4 with a 15-minute duration. Slots SL-3002 through SL-3004 already satisfy capacity_per_slot=3, base_capacity_per_slot=2, and is_overbook_capable=1, but the 08:00-08:15 slot is missing.",
  "decision_rule": "Create exactly one slot for 2026-02-03 08:00-08:15 with provider PROV-3344, clinic CLIN-01, visit_type_id 4, visit_mode in_person, capacity_per_slot 3, base_capacity_per_slot 2, and is_overbook_capable 1. Do not redundantly update the three compliant slots. After creation succeeds, create the booking on any qualifying slot with remaining capacity, explicitly setting patient_id=2, status=scheduled, visit_type_id=4, and is_same_day_booking=1.",
  "expected_transition": "The interval contains four contiguous 15-minute overbook-capable slots from 08:00 through 09:00, followed by a scheduled Same-day Sick Visit booking for Maria Lopez whose is_same_day_booking value is 1.",
  "recovery_check": "Re-list slots for the interval and confirm all four quarter-hour periods exist with base capacity 2 and current capacity 3. After booking, inspect the returned booking or call get_booking and verify the patient, provider, clinic, visit type, status, selected slot, and is_same_day_booking=1; do not report completion if the same-day flag is 0."
}

